  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Smt Rekha vs Sri D Suresh on 22 January, 2016 Bench: N.K.Patil, S.Sujatha",
    "facts": "During the pendency of the said appeal the husband respondent herein filed petition for divorce Under Section XIII(1- A) (II) of the Hindu Marriage Act in M.C.No.4375/2011 and the said Petition also decided in favour of the respondent on 28.10.2013 against which the appellant wife filed appeal before this Hon'ble Court in M.F.A No.10214/2013 and both the appeals are pending consideration. Since the children are with the custody of the appellant wife and residing nearby the school which the children are studying in 9th standard. The respondent husband agreed for the same. B) After completion of the SSLC examination of the children the respondent agreed to join the company of her husband along with children Bhavya and Bharath, in the event the appellant wife failed to join the company of the husband along with the children immediately a week after the SSLC Examination in the year 2017, the Respondent Husband is at liberty to take the Children Bhavya and Bharath to his custody and looking after them by providing education, food, clothes and other daily Needs. C) The Respondent husband agreed to pay the maintenance as ordered by the Family Court at Bangalore C.Misc.No.152/2010 till the completion of the SSLC Examination of the Children in the year 2017, further the respondent husband agreed to pay the academic education expenses till the respondent took the children into his custody and also agreed to pay the arrears of maintenance from the month of July, 2015 to end of December 2015 a sum of Rs,12000/- (Rupees Twelve Thousand) @ Rs.2,000/-P.M, the education expenses for SSLC would be paid by the respondent subject to production of relevant bills.",
    "arguments": "",
